{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>If you shall come to the land.</b> This utterance was to Moses and to Aaron together, that they should say thus to Israel, as He mentioned, 'speak to them.'" "<b>And it is fitting</b> to say that since the utterance of this passage came to both of them, they are included in 'if you shall come to the land'; and He hinted to them that they would not enter the land, just as Moses himself hinted (ibid. 15), 'you will bring them and plant them,' excluding himself from their number. And even though Moses and Aaron were now complete righteous men and had not sinned, on account of the honor of Israel they did not wish to enter the land and died in the wilderness. Scripture wished to hint that even the righteous leaders were destined to die there, and their merit would not prevail so that they would enter the land. And to include further in this hint: just as they died — and Moses and Aaron with them — in the wilderness and did not merit to enter the land, so they are destined to be raised in the resurrection of the dead, and Moses and Aaron with them, and they will bring them into the land and be their shepherds as at first, and their counselors as at the beginning, with an ascent of attainment greater than what they had in the wilderness — because Moses in his lifetime yearned to enter the land and to fulfill the commandments that depend upon it, which he could not fulfill outside the land; therefore he will merit the resurrection of the dead, and his soul will attain the perfection and attainment worthy of one who fulfills all the commandments, every one. And likewise Israel of that generation who died in the wilderness — they are the very ones who received the Torah and saw the holy assembly and the vision of the glory of HaShem, eye to eye; since they received their punishment, they will merit the resurrection of the dead and will be elevated in attainment and in great excellence more than what they were."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:32.069716737Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}